<div id="S5.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Impact of LLM Models. </span> To justify our modular model selection strategy, we evaluate the performance of various LLM backbones across the two module (<span id="S5.SS3.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">FCG Generation</span> and <span id="S5.SS3.p7.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">User Prompt Synthesis</span>) of <span id="S5.SS3.p7.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">AgentRaft</span>. As summarized in <a href="#S5.T7" title="In 5.3. RQ2: Effectiveness of Individual Components ‣ 5. Evaluation ‣ AgentRaft: Automated Detection of Data Over-Exposure in LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, candidate models exhibit distinct advantages based on the specific cognitive requirements of each task. For <span id="S5.SS3.p7.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">FCG Construction</span>, which requires precise logical mapping of tool dependencies, DeepSeek-V3.2 achieves a peak F1 score of 97.22% and identifies all 94 vulnerable call chains. Conversely, Qwen3-Plus demonstrates superior efficacy in <span id="S5.SS3.p7.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">User Prompt Synthesis</span>, attaining a trigger coverage of 92.34% and generating 321 valid prompts that successfully trigger DOE.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T7" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7. </span>Effectiveness of each individual module in different LLM models (Enterprise scenario).</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
