<td id="S5.T7.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="S5.T7.2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">Qwen3-Plus<sup id="S5.T7.2.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">‡</sup></span></td>
<td id="S5.T7.2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="S5.T7.2.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">88.10</span></td>
<td id="S5.T7.2.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="S5.T7.2.1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">86</span></td>
<td id="S5.T7.2.1.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="S5.T7.2.1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:50%;">92.34</span></td>
<td id="S5.T7.2.1.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="S5.T7.2.1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:50%;">321</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T7.2.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T7.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="S5.T7.2.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">DeepSeek-V3.2<sup id="S5.T7.2.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">†</sup></span></td>
<td id="S5.T7.2.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="S5.T7.2.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:50%;">97.22</span></td>
<td id="S5.T7.2.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="S5.T7.2.1.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:50%;">94</span></td>
<td id="S5.T7.2.1.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="S5.T7.2.1.5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">79.50</span></td>
<td id="S5.T7.2.1.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="S5.T7.2.1.5.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">245</span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S5.T7.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left ltx_figure_panel"><span id="S5.T7.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">Note: <sup id="S5.T7.3.1.1" class="ltx_sup">†</sup>Selected for Call Graph Construction; <sup id="S5.T7.3.1.2" class="ltx_sup">‡</sup>Selected for User Prompt Generation. Bold values represent the peak performance that justifies our modular model selection strategy.</span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">This performance divergence further underscores the structural necessity of both the FCG and User Prompt Synthesis modules within the <span id="S5.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">AgentRaft</span> framework. Since DOE detection operates as a sequential pipeline, the final auditing effectiveness is strictly bounded by the fidelity of the FCG and the coverage of the user prompt execution. Specifically, low FCG accuracy would lead to an incomplete identification of potential attack paths, causing the system to overlook deep-seated risks (False Negatives). Similarly, insufficient prompt coverage would fail to activate and verify even the correctly identified risks during runtime. Therefore, the modular employment of specialized models is essential to ensure that neither stage becomes a bottleneck, thereby maximizing the end-to-end detection rate of complex privacy risks in LLM Agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.SS3.p9.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="111.5" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 111.5" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,111.5) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 111.5 L 477.38 111.5 L 477.38 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 0.69 L 0.69 110.81 L 476.68 110.81 L 476.68 0.69 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.55 10.09)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.83em;--ltx-fo-height:6.79em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="96.71" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 94.02)" width="454.27"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.SS3.p9.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.83em;">
<span id="S5.SS3.p9.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="S5.SS3.p9.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p9.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Takeaway for RQ2. </span><span id="S5.SS3.p9.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
The evaluation demonstrates that each constituent module of </span><span id="S5.SS3.p9.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">AgentRaft</span><span id="S5.SS3.p9.pic1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> achieves high-fidelity performance across all metrics, collectively establishing a robust and effective pipeline for systematic Data Over-exposure detection.</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2603.07557v1/baseline_compare.png" id="S5.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/205;" width="333" height="205" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6. </span>DOE detection under different method (User prompt generation and over-exposure judge).</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S5.F6.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left ltx_figure_panel"><span id="S5.F6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">Note: This evaluation focuses on the <span id="S5.F6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Enterprise Collaboration</span> scenario, contains <span id="S5.F6.2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">94</span> ground-truth call chains involving DOE.</span></p></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4. </span>RQ3: Comparison with Baseline Approach</h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline Setting. </span> To isolate the contribution of each core component, we define three baseline configurations and evaluate them against <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">AgentRaft</span> within the <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Enterprise Collaboration</span> scenario, which contains 94 ground-truth DOE risks (call chain level). We select one scenario for the cost consideration instead of all four scenarios and also because our framework is fundamentally scenario-agnostic. The baselines are structured as: (1) <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline 1</span> (Random prompt generation by LLM + Single-LLM judge); (2) <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline 2</span> (Random prompt generation by LLM + Multi-LLM voting judge); and (3) <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline 3</span> (CG-guided prompt synthesis + Single-LLM judge). We choose GPT-4.1 for the single-LLM judge. The comparison result is shown in <a href="#S5.F6" title="In 5.3. RQ2: Effectiveness of Individual Components ‣ 5. Evaluation ‣ AgentRaft: Automated Detection of Data Over-Exposure in LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User Prompt Generation. </span> The results highlight the critical role of the Function Call Graph (FCG) in navigating the Agent’s tool-use logic. Without the structural guidance of FCG, Baseline 1 and 2 fail to activate deep-seated logical call chains, capturing only approximately 18–20% of risks even after 300 prompts. In contrast, <span id="S5.SS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">AgentRaft</span> demonstrates superior discovery efficiency, capturing 69.15% of ground-truth DOE instances within the first 50 prompts. This underscores that FCG-guided synthesis effectively optimizes the search space, allowing for the rapid generation of high-quality test user prompts that target complex multi-tool sequences.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Over-Exposure Judge. </span> The necessity of the consensus-based identification is evidenced by the gap between <span id="S5.SS4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">AgentRaft</span> and Baseline 3. While Baseline 3 benefits from CG-guided synthesis, its discovery rate plateaus at approximately 76.6% due to the inherent reasoning errors and hallucinations of a single-model judge. <span id="S5.SS4.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">AgentRaft</span> overcomes this bottleneck through the multi-LLM voting committee, achieving near-total coverage (<math id="S5.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>99%) at 150 prompts. These findings confirm that while FCG is essential for call chain activation, the voting mechanism is crucial for reducing identification noise and ensuring high-precision DOE risk verification in diverse Agent environments.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.SS4.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="94.89" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 94.89" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,94.89) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 94.89 L 477.38 94.89 L 477.38 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 0.69 L 0.69 94.2 L 476.68 94.2 L 476.68 0.69 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.55 10.09)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.83em;--ltx-fo-height:5.59em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="80.1" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 77.41)" width="454.27"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S5.SS4.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.83em;">
<span id="S5.SS4.p4.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="S5.SS4.p4.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p4.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Takeaway for RQ3. </span><span id="S5.SS4.p4.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
The comparative analysis demonstrates that the synergy between FCG-guided call chain activation and multi-LLM consensus is essential for achieving high detection coverage, as it significantly outperforms random search and single-model baselines in discovering deep-seated DOE risks.</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T8" class="ltx_table">

