<p id="A2.T10.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left ltx_figure_panel"><span id="A2.T10.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">Note: A single tool may be categorized into multiple scenarios. Therefore, the total ratio exceeds 100%.</span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We have analyzed the scenarios of MCP tools in the market, and Table <a href="#A2.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix Appendix B Evaluation ‣ AgentRaft: Automated Detection of Data Over-Exposure in LLM Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> presents the distribution of application scenarios of tools from the third-party tool market. It can be observed that Data Management &amp; Analysis (58.5%), Software Dev &amp; IT Ops (56.6%), Enterprise Collaboration (39.8%), and Social Platform Comm. (21.7%) are the primary application directions of tools in the market.</p>
</div>
